#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/id #uuid "4031c8a9-0559-5d8d-a1a5-6e3402c19b27" :question/math-academy-id "e-26133" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids ![](images/df/df720fc5b6471db8190154ad9e8c1a3094f3fe885f6150de21bb7a5ef0653be5.svg) and ![](images/ea/ea8dbe9b1e82824b527a7f87153b0ef9aa33e6af2f9f48ff5377b4ad19b48c2b.svg) whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n![](images/7c/7cf42f88ef110c2dea6d3ab150ed095c8845a4b3a110ae955e1c1da666bcc364.svg)\n\nFind ![](images/46/4694851f2a7762e81f5ff1328018557fee878a018c60f2b8db8be5b9775f24ee.svg) ![](images/65/65537e63a2f6c671139d4145c5157b89d95c0f6db5a0304d39f3aa0ee781a4a1.svg) and ![](images/ae/ae992fcbb9b6e797b7a06dda4dbedec893ebad102944c504a0de22790e75e940.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the ![](images/d4/d43a228fcfe8f3eeb60a2ce9ec2d0cca2ebd281c09cceef580587e8ef5672511.svg)-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n![](images/f9/f94b2d4acca3dae2e05ff1cc1ba860488de8ca4fd3b1468bf2f0287ac8fd208b.svg)\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the ![](images/d4/d43a228fcfe8f3eeb60a2ce9ec2d0cca2ebd281c09cceef580587e8ef5672511.svg)-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region:\n![](images/28/28f530c26d2a007471d7419a705b33a62378348c0bbfa9fab6f79e2aa0fa5fb2.svg)\nwhere ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) is the interior of the circle ![](images/1d/1d4b64030885f51b4f44e80010686c07bdb3e8d88386271543d08b91e6ad9d75.svg)\n\nAs a result, the volume of ![](images/08/085f4d77675f3cb7323d94feaa9eaa38f2fecb26c0f8483895f9ddf36b8d319d.svg) is given by\n![](images/00/0066a0d710b1f0a807ed0ece319744c6d826d0f7af56f8db4b88d8cb8ea3f652.svg)\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) consists of\n\n- the lower part ![](images/68/687143de30f2e07f089e3e2d728d31db586a552ab6e9694dccb0612e0b6b6fa9.svg) and\n\n- the upper part ![](images/a1/a150d3381edb05cce1fdbbaf82b7364009114579fe1b0e647d004bff51b47d75.svg)\n\nfor ![](images/22/225fcd90b7a79b6f4559894a4ec6ffd00aa643ee0c83719e6ebd165764497f81.svg)\n\nTherefore, we have\n![](images/11/11b70e034ca321a0eeabaeac26e55564ef04951147a69d158a23795b4cd0d0c9.svg)\n\nSo,\n![](images/df/dfe19692ea883c7962ae2f7b539263c064afbab0012d5e9238f0046384de56b7.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129024 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "7dcea6be-fd16-5312-b50c-157bafcc2d65" :question/math-academy-id "e-8189" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR = \\Big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{2y}, \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq yz \\Big\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}{\\int }_{0}^{yz}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}[x]_{x=0}^{x=yz}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}yz\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y{[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{2y}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{y}{2}{(\\sqrt{2y})}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(8-1)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129025 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "b0ad2f24-6f0c-5d66-9312-5e41840b4fe5" :question/math-academy-id "e-8190" :question/problem "![](images/04/043adf0ef683c24fbf4680145411d86fa94b52016bee44ac8f08ca7c5ca9f1b7.png)\n\n \n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/75/75a76a2dbc34c889335e66623e12b686eb9a255ee0d67f9be0e3792f2650360c.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (x,y) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/e1/e19ffe6a0555851c2b05526272beb21dbcdc082a23a2e11809c661666efdf133.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-x-y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-x-y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(4-x)y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}((4-x)(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6-2x\\,dx \\\\  & =[6x-{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(6(1)-{1}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129026 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/id #uuid "7883263b-110b-558f-83b2-0f6ec28be2c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-8191" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the surface ![](images/9c/9c7c9aac6c94031d8430a8e8a2e4d3678a640379cdbc173fc5209ea532f3191b.svg) the plane ![](images/6c/6c78648d93eec934cde0f90387e06783c3d777a7a445e39afc2e5fa91bc2ec0c.svg) and the planes ![](images/89/89c97ad93c125fc2b6f61d44fe9a90845fd289329d79d506c857f970d7586540.svg) ![](images/36/36fdd3a0fb618d9692c52fd9bcb6e916441dee88dbce405fb885ec0f7782f047.svg) ![](images/6b/6be447d259b9b63c2cdd7adc4107d7c96ed4df1730890fc1bb5ce7cd585b8ea6.svg) ![](images/e0/e0f55ae8b32c4b9d5e58808c159b7433fd6e5b9db2212ecdf719869ea230a010.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type III region.\n\nFor each point ![](images/49/494198ee647d85e4442556a23f0c2d56aa601367360c321385ffc94523c47d73.svg) in the rectangular base region\n![](images/2d/2d0c4af57f0ba5e29300533e6ab0d95ce702b9d75bf175cbb9ffdca5f371d634.svg)\nthe variable ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) runs from the surface\n![](images/72/72a6a2c2ba533fff74fe6ff80bafa9db62c3cbbc81f8be01cb7f5846b95f8dc8.svg)\nup to the plane\n![](images/36/3692729086c0564b65a7865e92dc2d5930f72b59abc0ea7634cd6dfa539b71b1.svg)\n\nSo we can write:\n![](images/d7/d7f58e8932311896757dffef5a240cb53a2b5e0b439455dbf83be832c8c15a01.svg)\n\nTherefore, the volume of ![](images/08/085f4d77675f3cb7323d94feaa9eaa38f2fecb26c0f8483895f9ddf36b8d319d.svg) is given by the following triple integral:\n\n![](images/1e/1e0c7ab5158a2e2dab67f2efae6ef29ac6be9e38bb9613c9c00a96d24c377a93.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ec6ec01-733e-5f02-af23-9cc8caaac3a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412118} {:answer/id #uuid "7908b9c9-85f1-5fb7-8993-c1b1c1be6014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412124} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a79b99-32b0-5d67-90f5-be49d7031cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412146} {:answer/id #uuid "bc206240-eb24-501d-9e9e-fc7fd50a7902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412147} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ffd103-8f74-5398-842a-0cf2cb86197a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc206240-eb24-501d-9e9e-fc7fd50a7902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412147} :answer-field/id #uuid "3acdc6ec-2a12-547a-88f2-73cc8411f0a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89162549-49ec-507f-b56c-dea9e66a6c30" :question/math-academy-id "q-161654" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1-x\\le y\\le 1+x,\\,0\\le z\\le xy\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}{\\int }_{0}^{xy}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}[z]_{z=0}^{z=xy}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}xy\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1-x}^{y=1+x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}((1+x)^{2}-(1-x)^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}((1+2x+{x}^{2})-(1-2x+{x}^{2}))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}(4x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67f82f56-56eb-50da-97de-725200c155db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279536} {:answer/id #uuid "6c4ad352-64b9-54dd-94dd-8873c16622fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279574} {:answer/id #uuid "7c1575fc-c5d6-5681-a222-c312531d86dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279699} {:answer/id #uuid "7e681cf6-73f5-5a06-8d75-6c2b43284f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279727} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2262fc-6fd6-5c2c-981e-b4ebad86d0e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc2262fc-6fd6-5c2c-981e-b4ebad86d0e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280539} :answer-field/id #uuid "480daeae-2712-5e7e-a7fb-d3f6092574a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2cb18357-7f8d-5c17-b356-ff0cf34ef3fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161657" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,1\\le z\\le 3,\\,0\\le x\\le 2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,{[{z}^{2}]}_{z=1}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y({3}^{2}-{1}^{2})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy \\\\  & =8[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]_{y=0}^{y=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-8(0-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cc72655-a5c0-5188-8f58-5d27119d622f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278712} {:answer/id #uuid "83e8f582-51fc-5b6f-8d13-79e316ddc9df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279776} {:answer/id #uuid "8abac87b-8828-528b-bef3-d5a3fb2458f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279830} {:answer/id #uuid "c8cbb14f-9d62-5346-9b6a-32dbfa186264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280350} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a8e3e3-ceaa-5aa7-8afc-c5a4562508f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8cbb14f-9d62-5346-9b6a-32dbfa186264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280350} :answer-field/id #uuid "431b17e0-1868-5c68-b325-780074e18f9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "92ae0dd1-b6f7-54c8-bc54-cc5a6fb1fbb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161659" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}},\\,0\\le y\\le 2z\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{2z}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}[y]_{y=0}^{y=2z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}2z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{[{z}^{2}]}_{z=-0}^{z=\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{(\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}})}^{2}-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}2-{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[2x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=-2}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(2(2)-\\frac{1}{3}(2)^{3})-(2(-2)-\\frac{1}{3}(-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =(4-\\frac{8}{3})-(-4+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "343954e9-c53f-5136-9342-da031d631171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520872} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8618f2-a4c1-5463-ab9a-c3032c367b51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520980} {:answer/id #uuid "9cfbf36d-43f4-55af-88f8-c9911c1d33e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521120} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a41433-b3e1-5c92-a9c4-ccd8e0742151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521124} {:answer/id #uuid "ff83ce28-20eb-50da-bedd-918638dace6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "343954e9-c53f-5136-9342-da031d631171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520872} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a20ef1d-6ee3-5383-abac-10a8cde3ea7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b01530fa-080b-571d-ad1e-cd03aad8ce73" :question/math-academy-id "q-161660" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-{x}^{2},\\,-1\\le y\\le x\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{-1}^{x}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-{x}^{2}}[y]_{y=-1}^{y=x}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-{x}^{2}}(x-(-1))\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-{x}^{2}}x+1\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+1){[z]}_{z=0}^{z=2-{x}^{2}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+1)(2-{x}^{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2x+2\\,dx \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+2x]}_{x=-1}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{3}+1+2)-(-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{3}+1-2) \\\\  & =2(2-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6a5b58-75ec-53ab-a1d2-eb0bf32cf642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412092} {:answer/id #uuid "77a79373-1a09-54a3-a0eb-c907112d07e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412122} {:answer/id #uuid "9abd54bf-c0ef-5909-85ca-4e4eaf1cbed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412134} {:answer/id #uuid "b1cec824-ea51-56e4-b35a-71eecbf948d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412144} {:answer/id #uuid "fe6589a0-a2f1-5e12-abad-5d645468e2ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d6a5b58-75ec-53ab-a1d2-eb0bf32cf642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412092} :answer-field/id #uuid "e818f6e1-d129-5503-b9af-07473e5656ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9b5b7d1e-4726-5549-b494-2d265b26d8f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-161661" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,4\\le z\\le 8-x,\\,0\\le y\\le 2-\\frac{x}{2}\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}{\\int }_{0}^{2-\\frac{x}{2}}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}[y]_{y=0}^{y=2-\\frac{x}{2}}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}2-\\frac{x}{2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2}){[z]}_{z=4}^{z=8-x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2})(8-x-4)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2})(4-x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}8-4x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[8x-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=4} \\\\  & =(8(4)-2(4)^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}(4)^{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "546af882-b367-56aa-b818-8192ce2828bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279359} {:answer/id #uuid "b84ac7bc-b2e1-5cea-985b-2954b342f53a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280214} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9adf2c-2a98-58c5-8fd7-fb367df94817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280406} {:answer/id #uuid "d863e60c-d243-5dcd-a905-644d527833af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280503} {:answer/id #uuid "fba41283-2e57-54cb-b312-b32d1917aee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fba41283-2e57-54cb-b312-b32d1917aee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280796} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0016591-9999-5fe2-ae9e-6b503dd172a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a372c14-9ab9-5f40-9e05-8b6bd0720902" :question/math-academy-id "q-161677" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xy$-plane, the surface $z=4-{x}^{2},$ and the planes $x=0,$ $x=2,$ $y=0,$ $y=2.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-{x}^{2}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-{x}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-{x}^{2})[y]_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-{x}^{2})(2-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & =2{[4x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =2(4(2)-\\frac{1}{3}({2}^{3}))-0 \\\\  & =2(\\frac{16}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21737989-20b9-57bc-85fb-dd005e7013e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412086} {:answer/id #uuid "57a63e65-0af5-535e-921f-cf26a087a94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412110} {:answer/id #uuid "5f30f736-8249-5434-939a-dfd31765c473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412112} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5445c4-6f49-583f-8849-0c5d5fb4458f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412155} {:answer/id #uuid "d89e5e2c-05a3-56e2-a145-80c8cf2036a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21737989-20b9-57bc-85fb-dd005e7013e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412086} :answer-field/id #uuid "f31a7306-1b8a-5b78-bf95-372025264fa5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ddd03f9-52bb-5aac-ab6f-e8e23245dd8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161679" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xy$-plane and the plane $z=x+y+2,$ and the planes $x=-1,$ $x=0,$ $y=0,$ $y=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le x+y+2\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x+y+2}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z=x+y+2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x+y+2\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{[(x+2)y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x+2+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x+\\frac{5}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}x]}_{x=-1}^{x=0} \\\\  & =0-(\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32279d50-a3b6-5eba-856d-313b883aff63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279031} {:answer/id #uuid "5b984d57-3b7b-54d5-b4ea-cef9c93fad7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279435} {:answer/id #uuid "64ae39f6-2e51-5eda-8b64-894c74aff093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279507} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc3a27d-5fb8-5c40-bd31-08d84f6e5bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280243} {:answer/id #uuid "cf049f31-b01a-5943-aa22-682a2afc876d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b984d57-3b7b-54d5-b4ea-cef9c93fad7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279435} :answer-field/id #uuid "38728615-5df4-5969-b901-2f5cb9972327" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "58d3fcb5-6807-58ac-a1ca-bf0f74191add" :question/math-academy-id "q-161680" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the planes $x=1-y$ and $x=y+1,$ and the planes $y=1,$ $y=2,$ $z=0,$ $z=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,1-y\\le x\\le y+1\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{y+1}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{x=1-y}^{x=y+1}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y+1-(1-y)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2y\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y[z]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y\\,dy \\\\  & =[{y}^{2}]_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c00395f-9e82-5707-bf92-e864ad8edc0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412091} {:answer/id #uuid "4a4f7933-2872-53eb-b6fc-0e473411ef59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412103} {:answer/id #uuid "4b7b318d-9356-52d1-916e-d034ec92dd98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412104} {:answer/id #uuid "553eead2-a9e1-5860-9f23-0d10dc994fc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412109} {:answer/id #uuid "ce289eef-aceb-5a72-b3dc-c74255c1aae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "553eead2-a9e1-5860-9f23-0d10dc994fc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412109} :answer-field/id #uuid "5aa2decc-c0b9-5e4c-ba07-85849fb1c3ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "248b6467-c247-56b8-869d-ac65691d4383" :question/math-academy-id "q-161682" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the surfaces $x=-{z}^{2}$ and $x=\\sqrt{y},$ and the planes $y=0,$ $y=1,$ $z=-1,$ $z=2.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,-1\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,-{z}^{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-{z}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{y}}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[x]_{x=-{z}^{2}}^{x=\\sqrt{y}}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-(-{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[z\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=-1}^{z=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2-(-1))\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{3}({2}^{3}-(-1)^{3})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\sqrt{y}+3\\,dy \\\\  & ={[2\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}+3y]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{1}^{3}}+3(1)-0 \\\\  & =2+3 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c05b87c-0a2f-5b02-9732-195c4cebeb2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412084} {:answer/id #uuid "3efc03d6-4a00-528f-9d96-c985b96a5a27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412099} {:answer/id #uuid "52c8cce2-caca-5867-98e7-2a89cae75f20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412107} {:answer/id #uuid "d74a887e-50b3-566c-a5b5-055f90be3eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412158} {:answer/id #uuid "ee22bbbb-c1bb-5206-b091-b3f1ee42854b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c05b87c-0a2f-5b02-9732-195c4cebeb2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412084} :answer-field/id #uuid "77f278fd-49bc-544f-84b1-fa3bfe926285" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d44ebfc0-d493-5ede-9c33-adfa1ab81dd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161691" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0645201b3726750226811e0c714dc09d3075021fcbb6ddd1525748e9539c02d.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/c4/c4cf12ec9b53282620c1730f824c96d98e0b9dbabee0478bf258cf6c2741da81.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1+y+z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/b4/b497e6ef73b5b16e11baa08819e9628d3b5e1f2ee4d05fbafec48f73e087cbf1.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1+y+z\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1+y+z}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{x=0}^{x=1+y+z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1+y+z)-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}1+y+z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(1+y)z+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}1+y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}+y\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{2})-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b297e7c-d769-53ea-8c65-407ff3d71965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520782} {:answer/id #uuid "365194f6-bbdb-5806-b6cb-a366405227b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520880} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd533fa-b6df-5f0a-82f8-f039d177607d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521045} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5c1fce-95e2-5a1d-b0c8-18244b6208ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521151} {:answer/id #uuid "b1bd0eaf-67d3-50f4-afcf-748a5d55eeac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b297e7c-d769-53ea-8c65-407ff3d71965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520782} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb4d67ee-c5f9-5907-9389-cb8d07771ac8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f0b5299-7a35-5c1a-9b72-d6af14bd952f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161694" :question/problem "![](images/43/4315e0e20d37935d3f5454063475fdfa5ed7a1915f82ae96194e83880ba02e76.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/0b/0ba756dacf72b89b06c3c214e1582a74fa803f567082f57538e7a78c84d4591f.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2+x-y\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/65/65c61ad7dc2964cd0de9a6bbdf259fcf3388e25da4eaabf155d58ff0c05c8d55.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2+x-y\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+x-y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z=2+x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2+x-y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2+x-y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(2+x)y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2+x-\\frac{1}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3}{2}+x\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(3+2)-0 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15597838-21a7-5710-8d04-a20e27443d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278782} {:answer/id #uuid "344e23d8-bf2f-5fd0-b697-3782f28e621a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279043} {:answer/id #uuid "4017046c-69eb-5600-96f8-88b4ec6c8f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279157} {:answer/id #uuid "54859fa5-6b0e-5339-ab6f-784e6226fb8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279361} {:answer/id #uuid "cac6e4da-55a4-59b4-aec1-470bd96c890f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54859fa5-6b0e-5339-ab6f-784e6226fb8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279361} :answer-field/id #uuid "b05d6e1c-d362-5f58-a922-c7bdfcb8ad48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf85e5fc-e5a2-5308-98bc-5ce96212e0b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-161696" :question/problem "![](images/cf/cf19d77966b23604f18c4194b4166536ff2f12267cbc55a98a436bda9fc3c098.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/a7/a7261baec0c907779f5b1f5ff669ca826d4b93c5dd1b9a389e0989fe34756a6e.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-x-2y\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/65/65c61ad7dc2964cd0de9a6bbdf259fcf3388e25da4eaabf155d58ff0c05c8d55.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-x-2y\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-2y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-x-2y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-x-2y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4-x-2y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[(4-x)y-{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4-x-1\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3-x\\,dx \\\\  & ={[3x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(6-2)-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ab8e05-2f75-5f1a-81dd-e07557bc4267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412075} {:answer/id #uuid "18508c80-0e18-52e8-aaa1-c7e154a4a945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412083} {:answer/id #uuid "1c0c0737-e66b-54ce-a699-eb6eaa91aed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412085} {:answer/id #uuid "33546658-bf3e-5faf-af2d-8c9d52241a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412095} {:answer/id #uuid "adf7bc54-9182-550e-91a1-e85a8bb8a42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07ab8e05-2f75-5f1a-81dd-e07557bc4267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412075} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f638fd3-87cf-5489-b15f-bb90365aa5c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412186}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bc1d5c0b-7b74-5ad3-bb28-1b0236b6db17" :question/math-academy-id "q-161698" :question/problem "![](images/59/599b5392add89a6a22eb6c2232fedbdd26704ebf849bb05d7de52a6d81dcfb6a.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/59/599b5392add89a6a22eb6c2232fedbdd26704ebf849bb05d7de52a6d81dcfb6a.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{x}{2}-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/9e/9e7c6fad45d9d85bad5ca16a2000e4d44a1739ab70797e41ae94945a4ffb02ef.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{x}{2}-z\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x/2-z}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=3-x/2-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3-\\frac{x}{2}-z)-0\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3-\\frac{x}{2}-z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(3-\\frac{x}{2})z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((3-\\frac{x}{2})(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4-x\\,dx \\\\  & ={[4x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(8-2)-0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0186ed58-f7ec-5ef6-80f2-6bba068af8ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412073} {:answer/id #uuid "be2a6615-1145-511b-9323-6d645e89147a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412148} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f805af-86dc-564f-858f-cced5da9ea34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412152} {:answer/id #uuid "f263eb51-d454-599d-b9cd-c5c5f0283652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8+6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412166} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0bab28-2df9-528c-9c6b-acadde9b6b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+6{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7f805af-86dc-564f-858f-cced5da9ea34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412152} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca8f622f-5689-5e59-b05c-8fbe8f53d165" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3fb0f5ed-20e1-5a6f-bec1-d9ddd1ad73da" :question/math-academy-id "q-161703" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $z=2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}$ and $z=4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xy$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xy$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}\\le z\\le 4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}^{4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-(2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $y=-\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $y=\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-1\\le x\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}}}\\,2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =(2-2{x}^{2})+(2-2{x}^{2})+(2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =6-6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235407 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53753fd8-a2fa-534d-8c08-ab1807cffe31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-6{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234678} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e5070b-5fe6-54c6-b6e5-bbc3af44e243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}-6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234799} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a38841-5e3b-5330-b8c5-120f7073a26e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234876} {:answer/id #uuid "e2acf5fc-4990-5aaa-ae84-be72757a47ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-9{y}^{2}-8{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234900} {:answer/id #uuid "e2ec879b-7d5f-5abc-8284-8809e80a10d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{9}{2}{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6e5070b-5fe6-54c6-b6e5-bbc3af44e243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}-6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234799} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c9a9e9c-8c1a-5fea-8cb1-7b089d10977e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d129309d-a59a-5bf0-aa8c-890079ed6bb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-161706" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloid $x=3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}$ and the parabolic cylinder $x=1-{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{a(y)}^{b(y)}\\,f(y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $yz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =1-{y}^{2} \\\\ 4{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $yz$-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}\\le x\\le 1-{y}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the circle ${y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-{y}^{2})-(3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}}/2}^{\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}}/2}\\,1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}})}^{2}+(1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-4{y}^{2})+\\frac{1}{4}(1-4{y}^{2})+(1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b6bcca1-d72a-5f85-87c2-3550ef32d120" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234588} {:answer/id #uuid "1d4a2174-82b5-5949-89c4-c4fec08b7d1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-4{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234592} {:answer/id #uuid "2dcc9617-dc84-5765-a854-fb14efdac95a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-6{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234617} {:answer/id #uuid "54ad0bd9-e677-50c2-baec-fe8c3d2f7f16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+3{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234679} {:answer/id #uuid "93c413bb-1981-5c32-9f17-1d169b629607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-8{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93c413bb-1981-5c32-9f17-1d169b629607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-8{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234774} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9b78da5-f53f-57bc-9aa0-7ba1fa733f20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "12d08b78-b5d1-5179-8c7f-966d7d4e9314" :question/math-academy-id "q-161716" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the parabolic cylinders $y=4{x}^{2}$ and $y=1-2{z}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,z)\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2} & =1-2{z}^{2} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1-2{z}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the elipse $4{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}=1.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{4{x}^{2}}^{1-2{z}^{2}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-2{z}^{2})-(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{(1-4{x}^{2})/2}}^{\\sqrt{(1-4{x}^{2})/2}}\\,1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+(1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}+(1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2-8{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "553cda93-dcb2-5e16-b4c0-6ae818e9e098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412108} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8412c6-b5ae-5e4e-8894-ef77a1531b0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412131} {:answer/id #uuid "9081743f-8252-523c-aefd-cf033c9164c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412132} {:answer/id #uuid "9680b5da-cca4-55bb-9bba-6bb3fc907b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412133} {:answer/id #uuid "bffefc4b-533b-5a59-a2a7-3d67fb1ca1ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "553cda93-dcb2-5e16-b4c0-6ae818e9e098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412108} :answer-field/id #uuid "133b7b39-61d0-5df1-8fb5-ebbf0005ae7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c5e175a-7b49-566c-a1ad-cebab486783a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161741" :question/problem "![](images/da/daedf62c68ba62dee844cf17efc2d767da47a06ceccaedde854779f542b90114.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front and right ones, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7c/7c1738e97bc16a32f86d6901136afc4d9e288035d170fcd640db340ad36d19c5.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane.\n\nTo find the top boundary curve of $D$ in the form $z=z(y),$ we substitute $x=1$ into the equation $x=2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z:$\n\n$$\n1=2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z\\,⟹\\,z=2-\\frac{2}{3}y\n$$\n\nThen, we have\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-\\frac{2}{3}y\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/ea/ea8b8397163309a11aa478fcc21ab53ee293c19f0d77a93b5c3d3472bb0eba70.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-\\frac{2}{3}y,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3-z/2}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2-y/3-z/2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}(2-\\frac{y}{3}-\\frac{z}{2})-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}2-\\frac{y}{3}-\\frac{z}{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[(2-\\frac{y}{3})z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2-2y/3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}((2-\\frac{y}{3})(2-\\frac{2y}{3})-\\frac{1}{4}{(2-\\frac{2y}{3})}^{2})-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(2-\\frac{2y}{3})((2-\\frac{y}{3})-\\frac{1}{4}(2-\\frac{2y}{3}))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(2-\\frac{2y}{3})(\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{6})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3-\\frac{4y}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[3y-\\frac{2{y}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{27}]}_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =(3(3)-\\frac{2(3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{3}^{3}}{27})-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41180107-75c5-5623-b021-04c14a524c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234645} {:answer/id #uuid "46eb06c1-4baf-548c-9d0b-d97f5d6f46de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-8{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234652} {:answer/id #uuid "64222d8e-a20d-5b93-94a6-d92272709a1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-8{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234700} {:answer/id #uuid "95ccad89-ed14-5078-9ff9-12dcbe90889d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-6{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234779} {:answer/id #uuid "cbcf84c7-f9dc-53f5-8878-966091228f91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64222d8e-a20d-5b93-94a6-d92272709a1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-8{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234700} :answer-field/id #uuid "351f4c64-6f3a-578b-bb07-2d8260b8e536" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7682e487-9666-568f-b7a6-c77060041838" :question/math-academy-id "q-163221" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $z=1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ and $z=3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xy$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xy$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le z\\le 3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}^{3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3-3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})-(1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $y=-\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $y=\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}}\\,2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =(1-2{x}^{2})+(1-2{x}^{2})+(2-4{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4-8{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "019b4327-5ad2-57c4-991f-ae345072327b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}+\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412074} {:answer/id #uuid "834a8547-3c7e-58d8-acbd-c93cf9168259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412129} {:answer/id #uuid "af2f71bd-644d-5868-b8fa-2f4b088b1569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412140} {:answer/id #uuid "afcf7783-64e2-56a0-8cfb-04b04bdbf5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412142} {:answer/id #uuid "e14ce939-3279-5852-835b-269ab0e44698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afcf7783-64e2-56a0-8cfb-04b04bdbf5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412142} :answer-field/id #uuid "6365448d-1520-532c-a959-d9aa6da7c99c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d60206f-2159-50c2-97e6-e576ed41d216" :question/math-academy-id "q-38895" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xy$-plane, the surface $z=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ and the planes $x=0,$ $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ $y=0,$ $y=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f5010d-f686-51ba-a29d-c3e7ebee57db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27-27{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412077} {:answer/id #uuid "15b92e61-6c44-5617-9e76-b9e56e391b4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18+5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412082} {:answer/id #uuid "30e725ff-8723-507a-9752-9f42c6ef01be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18-18{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412093} {:answer/id #uuid "326b02ee-8bcd-58c7-ab55-05f61874238e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9+5{y}^{2}-5{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412094} {:answer/id #uuid "695a6dc7-cbc3-59a8-b915-157fba409c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25-25{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08f5010d-f686-51ba-a29d-c3e7ebee57db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27-27{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412077} :answer-field/id #uuid "067e6f74-92ec-5ad2-b12e-786bdf4c3f9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b5335202-1eb7-59f8-9c44-3e9c073e7a32" :question/math-academy-id "q-40319" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $x=5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}$ and the parabolic cylinder $x=9-4{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{a(y)}^{b(y)}\\,f(y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $yz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9-4{y}^{2} \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $yz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le x\\le 9-4{y}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $9{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}^{9-4{y}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(9-4{y}^{2})-(5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}}}\\,9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}})}^{2}+(9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =(9-9{y}^{2})+(9-9{y}^{2})+(9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =27-27{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
